inding modules: biochemical properties and novel applications</article-title><source>Microbiol Mol Biol Rev</source><year>2006</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>295</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16760304</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/MMBR.00028-05</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Shani</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Shoseyov</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modification of polysaccharides and plant cell wall by endo-1,4-beta-glucanase and cellulose-binding domains</article-title><source>Biomolecular Engineering</source><year>2002</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12103362</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1389-0344(02)00007-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Suurnakki</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tenkanen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Siika-aho</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Niku-Paavola</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Viikari</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchert</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trichoderma reesei cellulases and their core domains in the hydrolysis and modification of chemical pulp</article-title><source>Cellulose</source><year>2000</year><volume>7</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>209</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1023/A:1009280109519</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pala</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Lemos</surname><given-names